hrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.000399599938096657,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":99.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.20409,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.8,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":80.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"AEVEX Corp. operates as a defense technology contractor and enabler of the U.S. Unmanned Aerial Systems (UAS) dominance strategy mission. The company operates in two segments, Tactical Systems and Global Solutions. The Tactical Systems designs and manufactures battle-tested, autonomous, modular, and attritable unmanned systems, including UAS and unmanned surface vehicles with other mission critical products. The Global Solutions provides bespoke mission solutions, including AI-enabled airborne intelligence, surveillance, and reconnaissance (ISR), C-UAS, additive manufacturing, and specialized mission aircraft engineering, modification, and testing. The company was founded in 2020 and is based in Solana Beach, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Charles Roger Wells IV | CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $575,481 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 650 people. Revenue per employee of $666K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers. Stock-based compensation of $266 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). R&D investment of 6% of revenue (moderate) signals commitment to product development and talent.","financial_summary":["AEVEX Corp. is a small-cap industrials business with a $866M market cap on $433M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 25% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $106M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +12.0% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 11.0% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 20% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 1177% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":11.771292578217762},{"text":"Accruals elevated at +12.0% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Beneish M-Score flags potential earnings manipulation \u2014 a question of whether the reported numbers can be trusted","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"SGA costs surged 42% YoY \u2014 may reflect legal, restructuring, or operational issues","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $57.8M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-57814179.57},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Among the least levered in Industrials \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"AEVEX (AVEX) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/aevex-avex-q3-2026-earnings-074306000.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794470066.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"What AEVEX (AVEX) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/aevex-avex-said-q3-earnings-011239025.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794445959.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.318,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why AEVEX Stock Is Up Today","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/why-aevex-stock-today-224601771.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794523561.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"AEVEX Analysts Revise Their Forecasts Following Q3 Results","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/analyst-stock-ratings/price-target/26/11/63187024/aevex-analysts-revise-their-forecasts-following-q3-results","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794493619.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Why Is AEVEX Stock Soaring Thursday?","source":